  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "The four labels I, me, my, and we are fixed. Never change them or their order.",
      "Never put I, me, my, or we in the stem.",
      "Every stem has and plus <NAME> or a family word so the missing word is the second half of a compound.",
      "The gap is always the word after and. End object stems after and.",
      "Exactly one of I or me is correct. Drop the other person and read the stem again to check.",
      "Keep the pool near half subject I and half object me.",
      "my and we are never correct in this family. Do not write a stem that could take we.",
      "Kid world only: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands.",
      "For tier 3, use between, for, asked, or a time opener. No stem may work with both I and me."
    ]
  },
